
This illustrates computation of a full pmf for rotation
about the CC bond in 1,2-dichloroethane in aqueous solution (Nw = 500).
The full pmf is obtained by submitting just the pmfcmd file.
This will cause the running of nine windows with delta phi
= +/- 10 degrees with phi covering 0 to 180 degrees.

The only files that are needed to begin are
pmfcmd  pmfpar  pmfpar0  pmfzmat
Submit via
csh pmfcmd >& log &
or use the xPMFQ script for a queuing system:
xPMFQ dcepmf   (dcepmf is identical to pmfzmat)

pmfpar0 is used for the first window, then pmfpar is used for
subsequent windows. For the first window, the system must be set
up from the stored boxes. Subsequently, the last configuration
from the previous window is used as the starting point for the
next window.

The old way - 
Alternatively, one could set up 9 separate cmd files that
are chained together. This is illustrated with the d010cmd file.
I.e., the initial window is run by submitting the d010cmd file.
When it completes, it submits the job for the next window.
This continues until the final command file, d170cmd, is executed.
As another alternative, the nine windows could be run as separate
(unchained) jobs. In this case pmfpar0 must be used in every window
to construct the initial system from the stored boxes. Though longer
equilibration is needed, the nine separate jobs could be run on
nine processors, e.g., by submitting them to a queue.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

The energetics for the solute are evaluated with the OPLS-AA
force field. If one wanted to use AM1 instead with the CM1A
charges, all that needs to be done is change lines 4 and 5
in the dcepar and dcepar0 files to:
 QM method, charge calc & scale, solute charges:
AM1 CM1A 1.14  0  0  0


Time required: ca. 2.7 hours on a 2.4 GHz PC using OPLS-AA and pmfcmd, which
requests 2M configyrations of equilibration and 5M of averaging for each window.
The d010cmd, etc. files are set up for 1M/2M.
 

